  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABG: Realising the Faith Potential</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Located in the suburbs of Nairobi, Radio Waumini 88.3 FM is a Catholic Radio at the service of the Gospel. It is an instrument of evangelisation and promotion of all initiatives and activities of the Catholic Church in Kenya. The radio programme under the &#x2018;realising the faith potential&#x2019; project will provide forum for access to information especially to the most vulnerable of the society. 

The first strategy will focus on providing forum for access to information especially to the most vulnerable of the society. This accessibility is aimed at improving and fostering citizens&#x2019; engagement in leadership issues and creating a forum for expression. It is therefore planned that the common person will gain access to the studio and share in discussing leadership issues, invitations too will be extended to leaders to discuss issues from the theological, pastoral, political and civil point of views. All these will be done under the background of the Catholic Church leadership and pastoral guidance, with the key message of attempting to realise the potential of the Catholic Church in assisting to deliver accountability message to the leadership of this country.

This programme will invite Church organisations, civil societies and collaborate with parliamentary representatives to discuss those issues that affect the common man (used in generic form).   The forum will create a chance to communicate a strong message of responsive governance to Kenyan leadership.

The programme is expected to start running from October 2008 to March 2011. This will be a one-hour weekly programme with live call in, to seek clarifications of concern to the panellist.</narrative>
  </description>
